Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[" Section 1.2", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"1bddd2ce-b521-46c0-a51f-0b009fe5a741"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["  Conservation laws:\n  What comes out is what goes \
in:", "Subtitle",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3982871369974003`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"04b0a651-c858-44b4-9f3b-\
a5bcfacf94d2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Remove", "[", "\"\<Global`*\>\"", " ", "]"}], " ", 
   ";"}]}]], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3982871262174*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[215]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e3e503f6-3068-48f2-82a9-f5eb5ec1884b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Introduction:  The Basic Conservation Law", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"92ef01df-0724-42b0-aa91-a402288555d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Another frequently used application for ordinary and partial differential \
equations is the representation of conservation laws.  There are a number of \
physical quantities that obey a conservation law.  For example, the \
conservation of mass, linear momentum, angular momentum and energy in physics \
to name just a few.  Also,  conservation laws usually form the basis of \
modeling phenomena beyond the physical sciences.  The basic structure of \
these laws is of the following type:\n\nConsider a \"volume\" (often called a \
control volume) for which the amount of some quantity will be measured.   \
Thus for this control volume the quantity to be conserved will obey the \
following law:\n\n\t",
 StyleBox["Rate of increase of quantity = rate in - rate out + rate created",
  FontSize->14,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"81741170-a796-4fee-a5c0-4a2d2a2ad848"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Example 1.5", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6b76c5ff-d05d-45cd-8d46-28edbe3b8dde"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Conservation of mass", "Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3ed24975-41e4-4842-9290-57d03fff8642"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Consider a tank (control volume) in which water is flowing at a constant \
rate  k1 (volume per unit time).  \nAlso assume that the water evaporates \
from the tank at a rate which we assume is proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["v", 
    RowBox[{" ", 
     FractionBox["2", "3"]}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "281bd91b-2eda-416a-b44a-cabcea8cb983"],
 " (v = volume).  \nIf we assume that the water in the tank is incompressible \
then the volume of water ( which corresponds to the mass) will be conserved.  \
\n\nThe conservation law is as follows:\n\n\t",
 StyleBox["Rate of increase of quantity = rate in - rate out + rate created",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\n\n\trate in = k1\n\trate out = k2*",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["v", 
    RowBox[{" ", 
     FractionBox["2", "3"]}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6ae0fa5e-be29-49d7-b1c7-07c4bcebc01e"],
 "\n\trate created = 0\n\t\n Therefore:\n\t \n\tv ' [t] = k1 - k2*",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["v", 
    RowBox[{" ", 
     FractionBox["2", "3"]}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "92d4e7de-b55a-49d9-8e82-63d8911a2789"],
 ", \n\nwhere the constant k1 corresponds to the rate of water flowing into \
the tank and the constant k2 corresponds to the constant of proportionally \
for evaporation.\n\nIt is now possible to find if there is an equilibrium \
volume for this ODE. The equilibrium would correspond to a constant volume of \
water, i.e. v '[t] = 0.  Make this substitution into the ODE and solve for v:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982874012553997`*^9, 3.3982874120234003`*^9}, {
  3.463760237750849*^9, 
  3.463760244500719*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a9385f37-de2d-40b4-b0fc-\
f6b296066ece"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"0", "==", 
     RowBox[{"k1", "-", 
      RowBox[{"k2", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["v", 
        RowBox[{"2", "/", "3"}]]}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "v"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], "//", "TableForm"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982874203344*^9, 3.3982874696644*^9}, {
  3.3982875002424*^9, 3.3982875104184*^9}, {3.3982877948644*^9, 
  3.3982877999184*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[216]:=",ExpressionUUID->"06a64a4b-cd20-44f5-9926-814749b993e2"],

Cell["\<\
For our problem, the equilibrium point corresponds to the second solution.  \
Let's assign some values to the constants and analyze the behavior of the \
equation:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982875195424*^9, 
  3.3982875200044003`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3d85c04b-babd-4d89-be86-\
da372b71d31e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"k1", "=", "100000"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"k2", "=", "10"}], ";"}]}], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[217]:=",ExpressionUUID->"35435188-1118-4851-8550-bcf6c4888e2e"],

Cell["\<\
  Next find the value of the volume corresponding to the equilibrium water \
volume:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"098cd238-3029-4329-a1b4-c61fc6191e4c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FractionBox[
  RowBox[{"k1", " ", 
   SqrtBox[
    FractionBox["k1", "k2"]]}], "k2"]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3982875436144*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[219]:=",ExpressionUUID->"21ba786b-d0e4-4cd8-8cde-456ed1ced011"],

Cell["\<\
Next, look at a graph of the solution to this ODE.  The first case will start \
with an empty tank.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a50eeb78-5c41-4422-bbad-9fa7a7b30f12"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solutionRule1", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["v", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"k1", "-", 
        RowBox[{"k2", " ", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          RowBox[{"v", "[", "t", "]"}], 
          RowBox[{"2", "/", "3"}]]}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"v", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "0"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"v", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "100"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982875530044003`*^9, 3.3982875868454*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[220]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4c5bac39-d083-4ff6-8f24-25cb04b0d3f7"],

Cell[" Extract the solution using the solution rule:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b54d8f3-39c3-4b4b-9f75-b3e0bbe134bd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"v1", "[", "t_", "]"}], "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"v", "[", "t", "]"}], "/.", "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
   "solutionRule1"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[221]:=",ExpressionUUID->"97d28047-11c2-4ae0-9795-9b75d7321de2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"plot1", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"v1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "1", ",", "100"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotRange", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "1000000"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", ".01", "]"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3982876009224*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[222]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b55bc09a-d876-4c84-8112-e3ae87f86c8f"],

Cell["\<\
Next, look at a graph of the solution to this ODE.  The second case will \
start with a \"full\" tank.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fd2befb2-8576-4d46-9b12-43be238ce078"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solutionRule2", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["v", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"k1", "-", 
        RowBox[{"k2", " ", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          RowBox[{"v", "[", "t", "]"}], 
          RowBox[{"2", "/", "3"}]]}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"v", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "2000000"}]}], 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"v", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "100"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982876176464*^9, 3.3982876264504004`*^9}, {
  3.3982892075994*^9, 3.3982892111144*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[223]:=",ExpressionUUID->"38047b51-17d9-4c20-8ba4-aaa231c714ff"],

Cell[" Extract the solution using the solution rule:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8adc08ef-eca6-4d0c-b3a2-18a88c479170"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"v2", "[", "t_", "]"}], "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"v", "[", "t", "]"}], "/.", "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
   "solutionRule2"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[224]:=",ExpressionUUID->"bdabe39f-0738-4943-9c8b-078ad9fb3ec1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"plot2", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"v2", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "1", ",", "100"}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotRange", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "2000000"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "\[Rule]", 
     RowBox[{"Thickness", "[", ".01", "]"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3982876415654*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[225]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9217f337-3015-4e34-9c7f-32a9612ca149"],

Cell[" Finally, look at both solutions:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8cc89dd6-8569-4551-a225-b0a5483892eb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{" ", 
  RowBox[{"Show", " ", "[", 
   RowBox[{"plot2", ",", "plot1"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[226]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8b392281-71a5-4c31-a0f8-8ee5b9ce2e06"],

Cell["\<\
Observe that the above solutions are consistent with the equilibrium water \
volume for this problem.
The second plot \"plot2\" was listed first in the Show command because we \
wanted the PlotRange on this graph to be used simultaneously for both graphs.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fb6809ac-05aa-408f-978a-8933bd14eecf"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[" Example 1.6", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"84541684-9837-4d20-b095-c9c8d0db9c72"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox[" Organic pollution", "Subtitle"]], "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"dc484a7b-2e90-4541-bf5a-23eabb6b7f55"],

Cell["\<\
Consider an example of an organic pollutant that enters a lake at a constant \
rate, \[Sigma].  Also, bacterial action metabolizes (decomposes) the \
pollutant at a rate proportional to its total mass in the lake (this defines \
an ODE).  In doing so, the dissolved oxygen in the lake water is used up at \
the same rate that the pollutant decomposes.  However, oxygen in the air \
reenters the lake through the surface-to-air-contact (this is called \
reaeration) at a rate proportional to the difference between the maximum \
dissolved oxygen level that the lake can support and its current actual value \
(this defines another ODE).  
The ODEs become :

\tx1[t] =  mass of the pollutant
\tx2[t] =  dissolved oxygen level
\t\[Sigma]  =  constant rate of pollutant input
\txm =  maximum (saturation) level of oxygen
\t
 Rate of change in pollutant:
\tx1'[t] = \[Sigma] - k*x1[t]

 Rate of change in the oxygen level:
\tx2'[t] =  - k*x1[t] + k2*(xm - x2[t])
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"59961639-3d0b-48b5-9fd9-22543ce2da96"],

Cell["\<\
 Look for possible equilibrium points between the pollutant level and oxygen \
level.
 This would correspond to 0 values for: x1'[t] and x2'[t]\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"23e835fd-a69b-4e5b-97c0-d754f2f8edca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Clear", "[", 
  RowBox[{"k", ",", "k2", ",", "x1", ",", "x2", ",", "\[Sigma]", ",", "xm"}], 
  "]"}]], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[227]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2c91a839-f8e2-483a-a71f-87e2f538eb04"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Solve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"0", "==", 
       RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", "-", 
        RowBox[{"k", " ", "x1"}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"0", "==", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "k"}], " ", "x1"}], "+", 
        RowBox[{"k2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"xm", "-", "x2"}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x1", ",", "x2"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], "//", "TableForm"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982878374524*^9, 3.3982878421214*^9}, {
  3.3982892209014*^9, 3.3982892248634*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[228]:=",ExpressionUUID->"93216185-8d59-4ca2-8e35-37ef80343e9c"],

Cell["\<\
Observe that the above model predicts the existence of equilibrium conditions.

This system of ODEs is simple enough to solve directly:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"44539faf-9166-4b49-ac87-c187b444ed1e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solution", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"DSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x1", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", "-", 
        RowBox[{"k", " ", 
         RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x2", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "k"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "+", 
        RowBox[{"k2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"xm", "-", 
           RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x1", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", 
       SubscriptBox["X1", "0"]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x2", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", 
       SubscriptBox["X2", "0"]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}], ",", 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    "t"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982878676574*^9, 3.3982878724184*^9}, 
   3.3982879050713997`*^9, 3.3982879589934*^9, {3.3982892300514*^9, 
   3.3982892395884*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[229]:=",ExpressionUUID->"86321399-8e26-47c1-8f3f-004884d2ed8b"],

Cell["Display the solution in TableForm after simplification:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.3982873156644*^9, {3.3982879673534*^9, 
   3.3982879693764*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a2b95ab3-a44c-415b-9196-\
f1ec29ea5a3f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"  ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Simplify", " ", "[", "solution", "]"}], "    ", "//", 
   "TableForm"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3982873115114*^9, 3.3982879418684*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[230]:=",ExpressionUUID->"39beee0a-8ce7-4ffa-8aa3-55bf60f01d59"],

Cell["\<\
The above formula is too complicated to understand directly.  Therefore, \
consider some numerical examples.

Choose some simple values for our constants and analyze the system of \
differential equations:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d7965e20-7e81-468f-956c-c10ad28fad21"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xm", "=", "100"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"k", "=", "10"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"k2", "=", "20"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", "=", "50"}], ";"}]}], "InputOnly",
 CellLabel->
  "In[231]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7fd9c0e0-2255-4da8-8517-93eb9107068a"],

Cell["\<\

Let's look at a numerical solution for a typical starting value:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c4723ebe-8203-47d9-87ad-8d19b922e7e0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solutionRule", "=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolve", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x1", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", "-", 
        RowBox[{"k", " ", 
         RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["x2", "\[Prime]",
         MultilineFunction->None], "[", "t", "]"}], "==", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "k"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "+", 
        RowBox[{"k2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"xm", "-", 
           RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x1", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "20"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x2", "[", "0", "]"}], "==", "30"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982879874234*^9, 3.3982879949004*^9}, {
  3.3982892470594*^9, 3.3982892562874002`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[235]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c9187d69-7fbe-40a5-859b-6ff234e01a42"],

Cell[" Extract the two solutions from the replacement rule:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f9e6598d-fcd5-4891-912f-e9eddb0e13fd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"x1New", "[", "t_", "]"}], "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"x1", "[", "t", "]"}], "  ", "/.", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "solutionRule", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.3982880401764*^9, 3.3982880524954*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[236]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e282d29f-1e27-4c54-a4eb-20a19104dc82"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"x2New", "[", "t_", "]"}], "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"x2", "[", "t", "]"}], "  ", "/.", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "solutionRule", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.3982880636684*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[237]:=",ExpressionUUID->"75a238f6-9ecc-4f2f-83bc-79b3618d4eee"],

Cell["\<\
  Look at the two solutions, the concentration of the pollutant and the level \
of oxygen.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a8847bb-9a8f-4d3d-9bcf-1b809247942d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x1New", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"x2New", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
